se, and the average price versus the baseline.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Prefer shops that close at the median and stop walking away from lee-sungsoo", "what": "Lower the buyer\'s opening offer to about 90-95% of the median and raise it in one or two steps to the median, with the maximum 1.1 x the upper quartile cap kept. Rank 11im, lee-sungsoo, JangSeongWoong, dragonash first when their ask is at or under the median. Skip a shop for the item after one \'walked\' result there, and use the next one.", "evidence": "10 of the last 40 trades ended without a deal. Four of them are \'walked\' at lee-sungsoo with budgets of 160 (chair), 230 (bookshelf, twice) and 90 (lamp), where the median prices are 180, 260 and 100, so those budgets were below the going price. Also JangSeongWoong bookshelf budget 230 walked. Paid 82.9% of budget on average, so there is room. Reviews at the leaders show deals at 100 lamp, 180 chair, 260 bookshelf.", "expected": "Fewer walks and wasted visits, so a higher deal rate than 30 of 40. Price stays near the median.", "risk": "When the budget is below the median, no shop will sell. Then walking is right and the rule changes nothing.", "honest": "The buyer offers true amounts within its budget and writes factual reviews.", "test": "Compare the deal rate and the price paid over the next 40 trades. Count trades where the budget was at or above the median and still no deal.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
